WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.990
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:12.100
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.670
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:26.440
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:34.180
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.650
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.520
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.260
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:48.920
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.600
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:01.270
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.650
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:12.290
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:17.190
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:22.430
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:32.540
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:37.280
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.010
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.210
On your marks!

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.480
Get set!

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.830
<i>Takamachi-senpai!</i>

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:16.780
<i>Takamachi-senpai! 11.4 seconds!</i>

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.250
That's your best time today!

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.180
Great!

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.120
<i>Takamachi-senpai!</i>

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.850
Oh, thanks!

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:27.090
With a time like this,
you'll definitely set a new record

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:29.060
at the next
inter-high school competition!

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.530
You could probably even
get the world record!

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:33.730
Enough with the flattery.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.860
You should be out practicing instead.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.430
We're being serious!

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.230
Just look at all those college
scouts here to see you!

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.370
I can't go to college.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.910
I'm gonna take one last lap!

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.690
<i>Just how long can I
continue like this?</i>

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.990
Wait!

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:31.780
"Like a Swan"

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:44.320
Assistant Inspector Narumi
is up and ready!

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.000
Whoa, you got up all by yourself?!

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.740
Oh? That's not very polite.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.840
Is there something wrong
with getting up by myself?

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:55.810
Yes.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:01.310
It takes me longer to cook rice lately;

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:03.680
I switched to cooking it
with a gas steamer.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:09.050
That explains why the rice
seemed really fluffy lately!

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:13.390
Geez. This, plus your recent
habit of coming home early-

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.130
it really messes things up for me.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.790
Preparation is an important
part of cooking, you know.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.490
Oh, then excuse me...

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.070
Ayumu...

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:27.430
There's something I want to tell you.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.440
What?

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:36.080
All sorts of incidents have been
happening at your school lately.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.680
Please don't stick your head
into them anymore.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:42.680
They're police business.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.590
I know.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.190
I won't get in your way.

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:49.950
Good.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:58.440
You wouldn't care if they found out

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.890
that Kiyotaka was an
accomplice of us criminals?

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:08.230
<i>I can't let her find out...</i>

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:23.730
Outside the window,
kira kira kira ri

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:26.660
A shooting star streaks

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:29.100
Not that weird song again.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.800
-Hey.
-Yes?

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.840
Why do you keep following me?

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:36.670
Simply put, it's because
incidents occur wherever you go...

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:37.830
Stop playing around.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.370
Wait for me!

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.280
But don't stop so suddenly...

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.960
<i>Ryoko Takamachi-san...</i>

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:56.160
A 2nd year track ace and top athlete

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.860
who won the inter-high school
tournament 2 years in a row.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.830
What's that she's doing?

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.470
Oh, it's a game.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.740
It's popular among athletic clubs.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:09.440
One person throws a kids'
rubber ball at another person.

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.370
If it hits, then the thrower wins-

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.210
if it misses then the dodger wins.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:17.180
The loser has to buy juice
for the winner!

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.880
You get three balls to throw.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:22.450
The distance is probably
around 25 feet or so.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.120
You can throw the balls
however you want,

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:26.990
but it doesn't count
if a ball hits the person

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.720
after bouncing off the ground.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:32.560
Kinetic vision, sharp reflexes,

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.230
and explosive muscle
power decide the outcome.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:38.970
It's a really exciting game
for athletic club members!

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:42.110
But this is a little bit
of a prestigious match!

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:46.010
After all, the thrower is the
baseball team's ace pitcher!

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.750
I win!

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.870
Amazing!

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:20.310
She's not the two-year
reigning champion for nothing!

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:23.540
Her motor nerves are
at an incredible level!

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:28.740
But you can't say this game is
simply about motor skills alone.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:33.250
It appears the true nature
of this game lies elsewhere.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.230
That's not true!

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:41.530
Nobody in the world
could ever beat you!

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:45.270
I told you, anybody can
do it with enough practice!

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.500
Do you think?

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:48.610
Well, we'll see you later!

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.770
Alright, take care!

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:53.170
-We will! Bye!
-We will! Bye!

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:01.410
You appear to be famous in the
track and field world, Ryoko.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.790
Rutherford!

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.120
What do you want?

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:11.800
I get disgusted every time
I see your face.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:15.370
I need your skills. Assist me.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:16.530
I already told you!

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:20.600
I'll stay out of your way,
so leave me alone!

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:24.340
Before long, even more
dangerous Hunters will appear.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:28.980
To resist him, I need your skills...

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.710
As a fellow Blade Child.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:37.950
It doesn't matter to me if any
of the others get hunted down.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.450
And besides, I still
haven't forgiven you!

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:45.230
Yes. If only these guys weren't here,

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:47.860
he wouldn't have become a murderer!

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:53.770
It's the Blade Children's destiny
to have blood-soaked hands.

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:55.670
As is being unable to
dream about the future,

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:58.780
no matter how fast you can run.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:01.770
You don't look like you're
going to leave even if I say no.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.810
Let's decide it with a game.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:49.460
I hate using my head,

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:53.300
so we'll have a small match
of motor skills instead.

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:55.030
It's such a simple game...

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:58.370
But perhaps that's what
makes it so interesting.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:01.500
It's not the kind of game meant
for delicate pianists like you,

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:05.410
but if you want my help,
then you'll overcome that handicap.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:10.350
I'm undefeated in this game,
just so you know.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:13.920
Not even the baseball team's
ace pitcher could shoot me down.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:18.010
That's probably because he didn't
realize the true nature of this game.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.420
But you do?

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:24.730
This is no simple shooting game.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:29.030
Rather, it requires strategy
and judgment, much like chess.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.700
I'm not well acquainted
with ball games,

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:35.260
but I do know how to
put people into check.

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:40.110
You hit it every time, Kanone.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.380
Because it's a fixed target.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.450
With enough practice I
could do it blindfolded.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:48.690
With skill like that you could
probably hit moving targets too.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.280
No.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:52.490
In the case of a moving target,

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:56.330
everything is different,
even down to how you aim and move.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:58.360
It would be difficult for all
but the best sharpshooters

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:01.300
even with a rifle with
a high-performance scope.

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:06.840
Even the hunts my mother
took me on were difficult.

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:10.670
Wild rabbits not 15 feet from me
still managed to escape.

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:12.940
Forget about ever hitting any birds.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:15.850
Remember this, Eyes.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:18.850
You don't stop a moving target

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:22.650
with practiced skills or
your equipment's capabilities.

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:25.090
You read the target's thoughts
and lay a trap for it.

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:26.860
It's strategy you need.

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:28.590
It's just like chess.

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:33.100
Put another way,
you can still hit a target

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:35.160
even without techniques or equipment.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:45.900
Though nothing beats practice.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.120
<i>Kanone...</i>

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:56.480
<i>There is much you taught me...</i>

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:02.250
<i>I'll bring down a moving
target in three tries.</i>

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:31.210
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:33.420
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:34.920
I'm not really hungry...

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.980
Don't worry, snacks don't fill you up!

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:43.430
<i>By the way, what is the
true nature of that game?</i>

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:44.270
What game?

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:46.870
You know, the one they
were playing on the field.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:48.670
Oh, that...

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:52.510
At first glance, it looks like
a test of motor skills,

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:54.640
but that's not all it is.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.310
The game uses a light rubber ball,

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:58.750
so not even the best pitcher
could throw a fastball.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.720
A curveball would be easy to throw,

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:03.150
but it would be simple for an
athlete of Takamachi's caliber

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:04.950
to anticipate it and dodge.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:06.320
Hmm...

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:08.390
So if all you do is try to
hit the person on each throw

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.560
then they'll dodge it.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:13.000
If you sacrifice the first two throws,

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:15.270
you can force them
into an unmovable situation

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:18.230
and then get them with the third one.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:22.210
That strategy and judgment
is the main point.

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:23.910
I see...

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:29.780
<i>So if it were you,
how would you hit Takamachi-san?</i>

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.300
Good question...

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:40.860
<i>Alright, Rutherford!</i>

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.880
<i>How are you going to
sacrifice the first two balls?</i>

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.150
I'm ready! Bring it on anytime!

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:52.440
Ryoko. Allow me to tell you
something before I throw.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:55.740
I will not resort to collapsing your
posture with the first two throws

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:59.240
and then finishing
you off with the third.

00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:01.780
This is a prediction...

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:03.110
This first ball...

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:05.510
This first ball will bring you down.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:13.880
What is this?
Some sort of pathetic bluff?!

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:17.360
Let us begin the game...

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:24.900
<i>This pressure!
Rutherford is definitely different!</i>

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:28.740
<i>He's crushed his enemies
with this spirit of his.</i>

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:32.140
<i>Calm down. Anticipate his tactics!</i>

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:37.650
<i>Hitting me with the first ball
will be hard, no matter what.</i>

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:39.670
<i>That's this game's theory.</i>

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:44.950
<i>So why did he say he would
hit me with the first ball?</i>

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:48.860
<i>Why?</i>

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:52.730
<i>That's it!</i>

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:58.740
You sure eat a lot...

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:01.200
Potatoes are really good
at not filling you up!

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:03.240
So, what's your answer?

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:04.840
Oh, right.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:08.810
First, I would declare that I
would hit her on the first throw.

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:10.880
Is that even possible?

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.380
Just listen.

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:14.380
By doing so, my opponent's attention

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:16.790
would be placed on the first
ball more than necessary.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.220
I would then throw the
first ball straight up.

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:23.660
Instinctively, she would watch
the ball as it goes up, right?

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:24.890
Yeah...

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:30.200
When she does, I would throw
the remaining two balls.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:34.200
Even if she does dodge them...

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:42.410
The rules say you can use it as
long as it doesn't hit the ground.

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:44.610
So it would be like a fourth
ball to finish her off.

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:50.990
<i>Yes, the fourth and final ball...</i>

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:53.620
<i>My posture will have collapsed a lot.</i>

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:56.030
<i>There's a high chance he'll hit me!</i>

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:59.630
<i>So one ball is used as both
a feint and a finisher...</i>

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:03.430
<i>What a dirty trick.
Technically, he wasn't lying.</i>

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:06.440
<i>Because it's true that he'll be
hitting me with the first ball.</i>

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:10.540
<i>Plus he plays the piano
with both hands.</i>

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:11.970
<i>Meaning he's ambidextrous!</i>

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:14.280
<i>It's the best possible tactic.</i>

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:17.650
<i>But I'll be the one who wins!</i>

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:21.240
Bring it on, Rutherford!
I'll dodge whatever you got!

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:23.950
Can you, now?

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.480
Today's not your lucky day.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:44.100
<i>As I predicted,
this ball is a feint!</i>

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:48.040
You didn't let your
focus stray at all,

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.650
nor did you make any wasted movements.

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:52.350
You underestimate me, Rutherford.

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:54.510
I could see right through your trick.

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:59.540
No, you're the one who underestimated.

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:02.660
Ryoko...

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.390
Checkmate.

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:21.470
I predicted it. That the first
ball would bring you down.

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:24.580
<i>It wasn't straight up?!</i>

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:29.820
<i>He threw it parabolically so
it would hit me from above?</i>

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:32.560
There's no way you could
have thrown it like that...

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:34.420
You don't play sports

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:37.020
and you've never played
this game before!

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:45.170
<i>First time?! Was it really
his first time?</i>

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:51.210
<i>He saw that I wouldn't
easily join him...</i>

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:53.940
<i>He knew I would challenge him
to a match to get rid of him...</i>

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:57.000
<i>I'm undefeated at this game!</i>

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.520
<i>Did he check out my
surroundings beforehand,</i>

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:04.420
<i>predict my actions,
and then lay a trap?</i>

00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:08.490
<i>What's more, did he calculate
what I would anticipate?</i>

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:11.190
<i>I was certain I had
his plan figured out,</i>

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:15.820
<i>so I stayed still and didn't
let the first ball distract me.</i>

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:22.330
<i>That certainty changed me from a
moving target to a fixed target!</i>

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:26.680
<i>A psychological trap!</i>

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:35.990
I'll contact you later
with my instructions.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.720
Wait until then...

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.020
Hold on.

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:42.190
I made a promise, so I'll help you.

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:45.250
But I absolutely refuse
to murder anyone.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:48.500
I will not kill.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.270
Even if it's a Hunter,

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:53.100
I'd choose being killed
over killing someone!

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:56.510
I know...

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:59.070
That's why I need you.

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:02.940
I'm counting on you, Ryoko...

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:07.180
Are you sure you didn't
hurt your precious fingers

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:09.080
practicing your pitches?

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:17.030
You're like a swan...

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:20.100
Beneath the water's surface
you desperately flutter kick,

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:22.830
but you never let it show...

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:30.310
I really benefit a lot
whenever I'm with you.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:32.240
That's fine and all...

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:36.580
But are you sure
you're not full yet?

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:39.980
<i>Well, Narumi-san. Thank you very much!</i>

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:42.680
Walk me home again sometime, okay?

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.280
That's not what l...

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:59.770
There should be good things
for you starting tomorrow.

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:06.180
<i>Narumi-san! Narumi-san!</i>

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:08.680
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:11.350
Not so loud. I can hear you.

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:15.220
But today there's a new
2nd-year transfer student!

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:18.350
Transfer students aren't
exactly rare, you know.

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:22.920
But that's just it!
This is really bad!

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:38.210
Hey. Been a while, huh?

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:40.540
W-what are you...

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:44.510
Starting today we're classmates.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:46.000
See ya in class.

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:04.630
Kosuke...

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:11.630
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:18.330
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:36.490
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:42.130
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:48.040
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:54.610
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.610 --> 00:22:00.350
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:05.550
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:11.390
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:23.000
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:28.780
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:35.080
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:41.340
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:41.340 --> 00:22:42.640
Boxed lunches, boxed lunches...

00:22:42.640 --> 00:22:46.310
<i>Narumi-san's boxed lunches
make everyone happy!</i>

00:22:46.310 --> 00:22:48.450
A robbery takes place
in the next episode!

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:51.750
True feelings are more important
than pounded rice cakes!

00:22:51.750 --> 00:22:55.120
The mysterious thief Hiyo Hiyo
appears in this volume!

00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:57.660
On the next Spiral:
Bond of Reasoning...

00:22:57.660 --> 00:22:59.530
Unwelcome Visitors

00:22:59.530 --> 00:23:01.760
A friend in need is a friend indeed!

00:23:01.760 --> 00:23:04.200
True feelings are more
important than eaten rice cakes!

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:06.430
That's all for today's
Hiyono's Playhouse!
